  "Question": "The value of \\(\\log_5\\dfrac{(125)(625)}{25}\\) is equal to:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(725\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(3125\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A base-5 logarithm asks which exponent of \\(5\\) gives its argument. Since \\(125=5^3\\), \\(625=5^4\\), and \\(25=5^2\\), the argument becomes\n\\[\n\\frac{125\\cdot625}{25}=\\frac{5^3\\cdot5^4}{5^2}=5^{3+4-2}=5^5.\n\\]\nTherefore its base-5 logarithm is \\(5\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
